The user requests a global leaderboard of played games. Rank each
completed public tournament against the same fixed suite. List public
challenges separately in chronological history because opponents vary.

Existing records promised unlisted links. Preserve that behavior with a
false-by-default immutable public_listing field. New visitors explicitly
select public listing. Both challenge participants must permit listing.
The public index and qualifying replay commit in one Durable Object
transaction. Public reads avoid model requests and container startup.

All 217 Python tests and six JavaScript tests pass. Local browser checks
cover two pages and listing consent. Live enrollment verifies an 81-point
public tournament while an old unlisted replay remains accessible and
excluded. Another public game completed during verification, so live
checks use replay identifiers instead of fixed totals.

